# Beast Within: "Destroy target permanent. Its controller creates a 3/3 green Beast creature token." (CR 701.8, 701.19a):
# the destroy can be regenerated. Bot2 regenerates its Drudge Skeletons in response off its Swamp: the shield replaces
# the destruction, so the Skeletons stay (tapped) and Bot2 still gets the Beast, its target having been legal.
# A destroy that ignored regeneration would put the Skeletons in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Beast Within
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Black Lotus
Drudge Skeletons
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot2.Hand.Drudge Skeletons.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Beast Within.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Drudge Skeletons)
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Drudge Skeletons.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Beast Within; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot2.Battlefield = Beast Token; Drudge Skeletons; Swamp
Bot2.Battlefield.Drudge Skeletons.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Beast Token.Power = 3
